<title>FRANCE: EU cuts maize import tariffs to Spain, Portugal.</title>
<headline>EU cuts maize import tariffs to Spain, Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday awarded a tariff cut of 58.73 Ecus per tonne for imports of 32,000 tonnes of maize to Spain, France's grain office ONIC said.</p>
<p>It also cut by 51.78 Ecus per tonne the tariff for imports of 90,000 tonnes of maize to Portugal.</p>
<p>The EU's grain panel also agreed a tariff cut of 36.98 Ecus per tonne for imports of 1,000 tonnes of sorghum to Spain.</p>
<p>The tariff cuts are for preferential imports of grain from the United States under EU accession agreements struck in 1987.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
